# sky_day.fmat — a cubemap sky, as a material.
#
# A level's `sky:` block carried six texture names, a tint, an intensity and a
# rotation. Six levels sharing one sky spelled all nine out six times. Naming
# this instead is one line in the level file.
#
# Only the +X face is given: the other five are filled in by the <base>_px
# naming convention when the material resolves, and what the engine ends up with
# is all six spelled out — which is what lets the release packer see them.
#
# A sky material is the ONE domain that is folded into the level's own sky
# rather than overlaid at draw time, because `ease_sky` blends two complete sky
# values over time and a sky whose numbers moved under it would ease toward a
# moving target.
kind: sky
doc: Clear daylight.
effects:
  - effect: sky_cubemap
    px: sky_day_px
  - effect: tint
    color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1}
    intensity: 1
